{"v":1,"id":"sikagunite-gp","n":"SikaGunite GP","b":"Sika","u":"https://aus.sika.com/en/construction/concrete-repair-protection/concrete-repair-mortars/cementitious-repairmortars/sikagunite-gp.html","c":"construction/concrete-repair-protection/concrete-repair-mortars/cementitious-repairmortars","d":{"t":"One component Gunite dry spray applied repair mortar","s":"SikaGunite GP is a cement-based, ready to use, one component mortar. It is applied by mechanical application on vertical and overhead surfaces using the dry spraying process, and can be used in civil or mining applications.","a":["Easy to use with the addition of potable water.","Economical.","High resistance to chloride and sulfates.","Excellent abrasion resistance.","Controlled shrinkage."],"us":["Concrete repair of bridges, canals, sewer linings, sea walls, culverts and tunnels.","Pier and dock supports.","Sewage treatment plants.","Marine environments.","Retaining walls.","Protection of steel work.","Embankment protection and stabilisation."],"pk":"20 kg bag and 1000kg bulk bags on request","sec":[{"l":"APPROVALS / CERTIFICATES","t":"AS4020:2018 Approved for Potable Water Applications.","g":"Sustainability / Certifications / Approvals"},{"l":"Shelf life","t":"9 months from date of production","g":"Product Information"},{"l":"Storage conditions","t":"Stored properly in original, unopened and undamaged packaging in dry conditions.","g":"Product Information"},{"l":"Maximum grain size","t":"~ 2mm","g":"Product Information"},{"l":"Density","t":"2,080 kg/m3","g":"Product Information"},{"l":"Compressive strength","t":"1 day | ~ 20 MPa 7 days | ~ 50 MPa 28 days | ~ 70 MPa Material and curing conditions at 23°C / 50% r.h. Above results based on 50mm x 50mm cube @ 0.113 w/p ratio","g":"Technical Information"},{"l":"Tensile strength in flexure","t":"1 day | 6.0 MPa 7 days | 9.0 MPa 28 days | 11.0 MPa","g":"Technical Information"},{"l":"Tensile strength","t":"~ 6.0 MPa at 28 days (Indirect Tensile) | (AS 1012.10)","g":"Technical Information"},{"l":"Restrained shrinkage / expansion","t":"≥ 2.0 MPa at 84 days | (EN 12617)","g":"Technical Information"},{"l":"Electrical resistivity","t":"28 days | ~ 89,000 Ω.cm 56 days | ~ 122,000 Ω.cm 90 days | ~ 148,000 Ω.cm","g":"Technical Information"},{"l":"Layer thickness","t":"10 mm to 175 mm approximately","g":"Application Information"},{"l":"Initial set time","t":"70 - 80 minutes approx. @ W/P ratio of 0.113","g":"Application Information"},{"l":"Final set time","t":"90 - 120 minutes approx. @ W/P ratio of 0.113","g":"Application Information"},{"l":"Consumption","t":"Approx. 105 bags per m3","g":"Consumption"},{"l":"Yield","t":"Approx. 9.52 litre per 20 kg bag","g":"Consumption"},{"l":"APPLICATION","t":"SikaGunite GP can be applied dry spraying process. In the dry shot process, the nozzleman determines the water content of the mix and therefore the quality of the sprayed mortar. A lower water/powder ratio can result in too much dust and a higher water/powder ratio can give a flowing mortar that will slump off the substrate. For applications to vertical surfaces up to 175 mm maybe achievable with overhead repairs up to 150mm depending on water additon. After spraying immediately screed off and trowel.","g":"Application steps"},{"l":"CURING TREATMENT","t":"Proper curing procedures are important to ensure the durability and quality of the repair. To prevent surface cracking, cure the repair mortar using plastic sheets, wet hession, or curing compounds such as SikaCure.","g":"Application steps"},{"l":"CLEANING OF EQUIPMENT","t":"Remove non hardened Gunite from tools and equipment with water. Hardened material can only be removed mechanically.","g":"Application steps"}]},"dc":[{"id":"d-ef06ff7998","t":"SikaGunite GP","ty":"product_data_sheet","tl":"Product Data Sheet (PDS)","v":"31/03/2023","u":"https://aus.sika.com/content/dam/dms/au01/r/sikagunite-gp.pdf","ok":true,"f":"PDF"},{"id":"d-083ad64a5e","t":"SDS SikaGunite GP","ty":"safety_data_sheet","tl":"Safety Data Sheet (SDS)","v":"","u":"https://aus.sika.com/dam/dms/au01/k/sds-sikagunite-gp.pdf","ok":false,"f":"PDF"}],"r":{"status":"published","ds":{"url":"https://aus.sika.com/content/dam/dms/au01/r/sikagunite-gp.pdf","doc_version":"April 2023, Version 01.03","pages":3,"sha256":"13ff6df32c4c6ecf9c225d905e232e0972309219c2c12bff53f7215fa9e751d7","listed_version_date":"31/03/2023"},"facts":{"consumption":[{"id":"sikagunite-gp:consumption:7ed0bd5b","label":"Consumption","text":"Approx. 105 bags per m3","s":{"t":"PDS","u":"https://aus.sika.com/content/dam/dms/au01/r/sikagunite-gp.pdf","v":"April 2023, Version 01.03","p":2,"pe":2,"sec":"Consumption"},"parsed":null,"calc":false,"at":null},{"id":"sikagunite-gp:consumption:e700e44f","label":"Yield","text":"Approx. 9.52 litre per 20 kg bag","s":{"t":"PDS","u":"https://aus.sika.com/content/dam/dms/au01/r/sikagunite-gp.pdf","v":"April 2023, Version 01.03","p":2,"pe":2,"sec":"Consumption"},"parsed":{"model":"yield_per_pack","amount":20,"unit":"kg","yield_min":9.52,"yield_max":9.52,"yield_unit":"L","basis_stated":true},"calc":true,"at":null}],"coats":[],"layer_thickness":[{"id":"sikagunite-gp:layer_thickness:37d0030d","label":"Layer thickness","text":"10 mm to 175 mm approximately","s":{"t":"PDS","u":"https://aus.sika.com/content/dam/dms/au01/r/sikagunite-gp.pdf","v":"April 2023, Version 01.03","p":2,"pe":2,"sec":"Application Information"},"parsed":{"values":[{"qualifier":null,"min":10,"max":10,"unit":"mm"},{"qualifier":null,"min":175,"max":175,"unit":"mm"}]},"calc":false,"at":null}],"mix_ratio":[]}},"tm":{"cure_times":[{"id":"sikagunite-gp:cure_times:55a0c19e","label":"Initial set time","text":"70 - 80 minutes approx. @ W/P ratio of 0.113","s":{"t":"PDS","u":"https://aus.sika.com/content/dam/dms/au01/r/sikagunite-gp.pdf","v":"April 2023, Version 01.03","p":2,"pe":2,"sec":"Application Information"},"parsed":{"model":"duration","min":70,"max":80,"unit":"min","qualifier":null,"at_c":null},"calc":false,"at":null},{"id":"